{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"acrid-incomplete-curassow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nThe live dogfood probe on Gerrit change 986 patchset 1 (revision d51c056d0b4859d1a5fcb311b311c4e531919078) received LLM-Review +1 at 2026-07-27 22:58:53 UTC with zero unresolved comments, proving the deployed reviewer ran. The commit contains `rebar-ticket: 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d`. However, the best-effort Gerrit voter persistence seam did not produce the required durable artifact: after a ticket write reconciled the shared tracker, `rebar search` found neither the revision nor Change-Id and `rebar audit show 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d --output json | jq .code_reviews` remained empty.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Reproduce and trace `review_bot.voter.emit_code_review_artifact` in the deployed Gerrit path, including tracker initialization/sync, exception observability, artifact creation, sidecar emission, and `relates_to` trailer resolution.\n- Identify the precise changeable cause rather than treating best-effort swallowing as sufficient.\n- Add a RED regression at the smallest real voter/tracker boundary, implement the fix, and retain fail-safe voting behavior plus actionable emission diagnostics.\n- Land through Gerrit, allow deployment, and rerun the live change-986 dogfood revision to prove a `code_review_result_v2` artifact is persisted and linked.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A live Gerrit review with a resolvable `rebar-ticket:` trailer persists one idempotent revision-scoped `code_review` artifact and links it `relates_to` the work ticket.\n- [ ] The persisted `code_review_result_v2` payload exposes `coverage.llm_ran` and the blocking/advisory/dropped/indeterminate data needed by the dogfood comparison.\n- [ ] Artifact persistence failures remain non-blocking for the vote but emit actionable bounded diagnostics identifying the failed stage.\n- [ ] Automated coverage reproduces the failure before the fix and passes after it without weakening existing voter tests.\n- [ ] The change lands via Gerrit with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments; the live dogfood probe then observes the artifact.","id":"5b09-4f3d-58cc-41e4","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["review-bot","code-review-artifact","dogfood","operability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review bot votes without persisting Gerrit code-review artifact"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785193392794342001,"uuid":"2706c319-30ae-47d1-ad6b-dc22ae44ce75"}